From 4398ffb7b3e41fe2b02cade57aecc1581113f63b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:05:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] feat: one sentence -> the whole replace, autonomously
 (replace_component)

"Replace the dishwasher with a new one that fits" runs a server-side job (server/replace_job.py)
on the run table and poll of "do the whole job" (runjob.register; GET /job/run/{id}):
remove_component -> measure_cavity -> scale_gap (when the gap is implausible for its kind and
the scale isn't calibrated: a standard 34.5 in dishwasher opening, 30 in range, 30/33/36 in
fridge, 34.5 in base cabinet; the standard that leaves the other axes plausible wins) ->
a search fitted to the gap (progress lines while it runs, the plain kind as a fallback,
150 s cap) -> the best fit, fits or tight only, within the purchase limit -> its GLB and the
next two's (assets.resolve_shared: one build per part; a proxy box gets one more try at a real
model) -> place_part -> job_done {kind: replace, spoken, summary, part_id, fits, total_usd}.
The follow-ups (next one, option 2, undo, put it back) work on the state it leaves.

Routing: fast-path phrases (replace / swap out / "X is broken, get a new one" / "take out X
and put in a new one" / "remove X. find a Y that fits" / "get a counter-depth fridge in
here"), and the replace_component tool for the LLM agent (offered when the scene has parts;
the system prompt names them).

The orchestrator's voice test (14 prompts on :8006), fixed here:
- p01: a provider failure (KeysExhausted, openai/httpx errors) is a "busy" reply with no
  actions, never a 500.
- p03: Whisper's "34 1/2" with U+2044 FRACTION SLASH, vulgar fractions and number words before
  a unit ("thirty-four and a half inches", "twelve hundred dollars") are normalised first.
- p09: "Remove the range. Find a 30-inch induction range under $1,200 that fits." removes the
  range, fits its gap (not the fridge's), keeps the limit (sentences split like "and").
- p14: "show me the gym model" is show_model {site} (server/sites.py aliases), not a search.
- p05/p06: the job never places a red fit; the step flow says how to set the scale when the
  gap no real part fits ("say 'the opening is 34 and a half inches tall'"), and so does the
  search summary.
- "undo" with a gap open is undo_edit (the headset's EditHistory.Undo).

